    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "PAA\nConquest\nof the Pacific\nMARCH 1938\nMASSIVE NAVY SEARCH MISSION\nOfficial Photo U. S. Navy\nAIRCRAFT CARRIER \"RANGER\"\nAAMC TO 1300\nVOUGHT SBU SCOUT AIRPLANE ATTACHED TO THE CARRIER\nU.S.S. RANGER",
      "APR\nAM\n19'38\nRANGER\nROADS-T.H, 1\n2012.149.2323",
      "LARGEST MASS SEARCH\nIN HISTORY\n300 AIRCRAFT\n75 VESSELS OF THE\nUNITED STATES FLEET\nThis cover carried in Plane No. 10 of\nScouting Squadron Forty-Two attached to\nthe U. S. S. Ranger which participated in\nsearch for the ill fated Crew of Patrol\nSquadron Eighteen Plane No. 7 under Com-\nmand of Lieutenant Charles E. Signer, U.S.\nNavy. Many Planes which participated in\nthis search including the one in which this\ncover was carried participated in the Navys\nsearch for Amelia Earhart around Howland\nIsland, in June, 1937.\n32\nMAR\n3\n11\nAM.\n1938L\nRAN\nUNITED STATES POSTAGE\nPORTER\nU.S.S.POWHATAN\nU.S.S.HARTFORD\nCOAST KAUAI\nA AIR MAIL\nLT JGJOHNSON\nUSS BANGER"
    ],
